# Express.js Backend Rules

## Server Structure
- Main entry: [server/server.js](mdc:server/server.js)
- Routes: `/server/routes/` - API endpoint definitions
- Services: `/server/services/` - Business logic and external integrations
- Config: `/server/config/` - Database and server configuration

## Database Integration
- Use Prisma ORM for database operations
- Schema defined in [prisma/schema.prisma](mdc:prisma/schema.prisma)
- Database config in [server/config/database.js](mdc:server/config/database.js)
- Always use parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection

## API Routes
- [server/routes/auth.js](mdc:server/routes/auth.js) - Authentication endpoints
- [server/routes/rounds.js](mdc:server/routes/rounds.js) - Competition rounds
- [server/routes/news.js](mdc:server/routes/news.js) - News management
- [server/routes/participants.js](mdc:server/routes/participants.js) - Participant management
- [server/routes/cityTips.js](mdc:server/routes/cityTips.js) - Location recommendations
- [server/routes/analytics.js](mdc:server/routes/analytics.js) - Analytics and logging

## Security & Performance
- Use helmet for security headers
- Implement rate limiting with express-rate-limit
- CORS configuration for cross-origin requests
- Input validation with express-validator
- Compression middleware for response optimization

## Real-time Features
- WebSocket support via Socket.io
- Push notifications via web-push
- Real-time updates for competition status